{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":2928212,"ns":0,"title":"Bauschinger effect","extract":"The Bauschinger effect refers to a property of materials where the material's stress/strain characteristics change as a result of the microscopic stress distribution of the material. For example, an increase in tensile yield strength occurs at the expense of compressive yield strength.","description":"Stress characteristics of materials","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}